PREAMBLE
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

No kid should be charged to learn.

Pythos is free educational software. It exists to give every
student, everywhere, access to high-quality mathematics and
physics tutoring without paying for it.

This license is designed around one principle:

    FREE ACCESS TO PYTHOS MUST ALWAYS BE PRESERVED.

Commercial organizations may include Pythos in paid products,
platforms, educational systems, enterprise software, and
subscription services. Commercialization of surrounding products
is permitted.

What is not permitted is any commercialization that eliminates,
obstructs, hides, or misrepresents a user's ability to access
Pythos for free at the official Pythos service.

If a company sells a product that includes Pythos, the company
must clearly tell every user that Pythos is free and provide a
direct, functional link to the official free service. That link
must genuinely work — without payment, without a subscription,
without a credit card, without purchasing the commercial product.

The rights granted by this license are conditioned on compliance
with its terms. This is a condition of the license grant, not
merely a contractual obligation. Use that violates these conditions
is not authorized and constitutes copyright infringement.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 1. DEFINITIONS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

1.1  "Pythos" means the software program known as Pythos as
     distributed by the copyright holder, including its source
     code, object code, documentation, and associated materials.

1.2  "Covered Work" means:
     (a) Pythos itself;
     (b) any work containing Pythos source code or any
         substantial portion thereof;
     (c) any modification of Pythos;
     (d) any fork incorporating Pythos source code or substantial
         portions thereof; or
     (e) any combination incorporating Pythos source code or
         substantial portions thereof.

     A Covered Work does NOT include:
     (i)  works that independently implement similar functionality
          without copying Pythos expression;
     (ii) works that interface with a Pythos Network Service
          through a published API without incorporating Pythos
          source code; or
     (iii) works that use only the outputs of Pythos (such as
           mathematical answers or explanations) without
           incorporating Pythos source code.

1.3  "Pythos Functionality" means the core capabilities provided
     by Pythos, including AI-assisted mathematics and physics
     reasoning, deterministic verification of mathematical claims,
     prompt-to-claim fidelity analysis, and delivery gate
     management, or substantially equivalent capabilities in a
     Covered Work.

1.4  "Pythos Network Service" means any system, application,
     platform, API, or service that:
     (a) is made available to users over a network; and
     (b) uses a Covered Work to process user inputs or requests,
         including through intermediate processing layers or
         microservices; and
     (c) returns Pythos Functionality to those users, directly
         or through intermediate systems.

     A Pythos Network Service exists regardless of how it is
     labeled (service, platform, product, tool, API, chatbot,
     application, or otherwise), and regardless of the number
     of processing layers between the Covered Work and the user.

1.5  "Official Free Pythos Service" means the free Pythos service
     operated by the copyright holder at:

         https://pythos.lanzar.me/

     or any successor URL designated by the copyright holder.
     The authoritative current URL is maintained in the canonical
     project repository at https://github.com/JonScott79/Pythos
     in a file named PYTHOS_FREE_URL. Operators who maintain a
     Free Access Link have a 60-day grace period to update links
     following any published URL change.

1.6  "Free Access Link" means a hyperlink, URL reference, or
     other functional reference that satisfies all the
     requirements of Section 3.2.

1.7  "User" means any person who uses, interacts with, or
     receives Pythos Functionality through a Covered Work or
     Pythos Network Service. Where a Covered Work is accessed
     through an API, Users include both the developers who access
     the API and, where applicable, the end users of applications
     built on that API.

1.8  "Operator" means any person or organization that distributes,
     hosts, deploys, or makes available a Covered Work or Pythos
     Network Service to Users.

1.9  "You" or "Licensee" means the individual or legal entity
     exercising rights under this license.

1.10 "Distribute" means to make available to others by any means,
     including download, physical media, hosted service, API,
     network service, embedded delivery, or any other mechanism.

1.11 "Contributor" means any person or entity that submits
     material for inclusion in Pythos.

1.12 "Complete Corresponding Source Code" means the preferred
     form of the Covered Work for making modifications, including
     all source code necessary to generate, install, and run the
     Covered Work, regardless of any intermediate compilation,
     transpilation, obfuscation, or other transformation applied
     before deployment.

