SECTION 2. GRANT OF RIGHTS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Subject to the conditions of this license — which are conditions
of the grant, not merely covenants — the copyright holder grants
you a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to:

     (a) use Pythos for any lawful purpose;
     (b) study and inspect the Pythos source code;
     (c) copy and redistribute Pythos;
     (d) modify Pythos and create Covered Works;
     (e) run Pythos and Covered Works, including as Pythos
         Network Services; and
     (f) make Pythos and Covered Works available to others.

THESE RIGHTS ARE CONDITIONED ON COMPLIANCE WITH THIS LICENSE.
Exercise of any right granted here in violation of the conditions
of this license is not authorized and constitutes copyright
infringement. These obligations are conditions of the license
grant and are not merely contractual covenants.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
SECTION 3. FREE ACCESS PRESERVATION — CORE OBLIGATION
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

3.1  FUNDAMENTAL REQUIREMENT.

     Any Operator who distributes, hosts, deploys, or makes
     available a Covered Work or Pythos Network Service must
     preserve free access to Pythos by satisfying ALL of the
     following requirements:

     (a) provide a Free Access Link as defined in Section 3.2;
     (b) not engage in prohibited obstruction as defined in
         Section 3.3; and
     (c) not engage in misrepresentation as defined in Section 3.4.

     These requirements apply regardless of whether the Operator
     charges for the surrounding product, platform, service,
     subscription, or software.

3.2  FREE ACCESS LINK REQUIREMENTS.

     A Free Access Link must satisfy ALL of the following
     objective requirements:

     (a) TARGET. The link must resolve to the Official Free
         Pythos Service as defined in Section 1.5. A link to
         any other URL does not satisfy this requirement without
         written authorization from the copyright holder.

     (b) FUNCTIONAL. The link must return a live, accessible
         HTTP response at the time a User follows it. A broken,
         dead, or incorrectly redirecting link does not satisfy
         this requirement.

     (c) PAYMENT-FREE PATH. Following the link must not require
         the User to provide payment, a credit card number, bank
         account information, subscription status, membership
         status, institutional affiliation, or any form of
         financial consideration to access Pythos Functionality.
         The complete path from the link to Pythos Functionality
         must be traversable at no cost.

     (d) PLACEMENT. The Free Access Link must appear in at
         least one of the following locations:

         (i)  the primary landing page, product page, or
              marketing page at which the Operator describes
              or promotes Pythos Functionality, visible without
              scrolling past the primary product description;

         (ii) the purchase, checkout, or subscription flow,
              before payment is confirmed; or

         (iii) within the product interface, accessible within
               one direct user interaction from any interface at
               which Pythos Functionality is presented to a User,
               not buried within menus, dropdowns, accordions,
               legal pages, or multi-step navigation.

     (e) ACCESSIBILITY WITHOUT AUTHENTICATION OR PURCHASE. The
         Free Access Link must be accessible to a User who has
         not logged into, purchased, subscribed to, or paid for
         the commercial product in any form. If the link exists
         only inside an authenticated or paid product interface,
         it does not satisfy this requirement unless it also
         appears in a pre-authentication, pre-purchase location
         satisfying (d)(i) or (d)(ii).

     (f) VISUAL PROMINENCE. The Free Access Link must not be
         styled, positioned, or rendered in a manner designed to
         discourage Users from noticing or following it.
         Specifically, the link:

         (i)  must be rendered in a font size no smaller than
              the smallest body text on the same page or screen;

         (ii) must be rendered with a text-to-background color
              contrast ratio of at least 3:1 (per WCAG 2.1
              criterion 1.4.3 or its successor);

         (iii) must not be placed exclusively within a navigation
              menu, dropdown, accordion, tooltip, or other
              collapsed UI element that requires a user interaction
              to reveal, unless the existence and purpose of the
              link is indicated by a visible, permanently displayed
              label at that location; and

         (iv) must not require the User to scroll significantly
              past the principal page content to reach it without
              any visible indicator of its existence in the
              above-the-fold viewport.

     (g) ACCURATE AND SPECIFIC LABEL. The Free Access Link must
         be accompanied by a label or surrounding text that:

         (i)  includes the name "Pythos";
         (ii) accurately communicates that Pythos is available
              for free at the linked address; and
         (iii) does not suggest, imply, or state that payment is
              required to access the linked resource.

         Examples of compliant labels:
             "Pythos is free at pythos.lanzar.me"
             "Access Pythos for free — no payment required"
             "The original Pythos is freely available at
              pythos.lanzar.me"

         A vague label that omits the Pythos name or implies
         a cost does not satisfy this requirement.

3.3  PROHIBITED OBSTRUCTION.

     An Operator must not take any action — whether technical,
     contractual, communicative, interface-based, or otherwise —
     that is designed or reasonably likely to prevent, discourage,
     or impede Users from accessing the Official Free Pythos
     Service. The following specific acts are prohibited:

     (a) placing the Free Access Link exclusively in legal terms,
         privacy policies, end-user license agreements, footnotes,
         or similar documents not ordinarily encountered by Users
         during normal product use;

     (b) placing the Free Access Link in a location requiring a
         User to be authenticated into or to have purchased the
         commercial product to find it, without also providing
         the link in a pre-authentication, pre-purchase location;

     (c) providing a link that routes the User through an
         intermediate page requiring payment, registration, or
         subscription before reaching Pythos Functionality;

     (d) providing a link to a URL that is not the Official Free
         Pythos Service and that imposes payment or restrictions
         on Pythos Functionality;

     (e) including any provision in an Operator's terms of
         service, user agreement, or other contractual document
         that prohibits, discourages, or penalizes Users for
         accessing the Official Free Pythos Service;

     (f) taking any technical measure — including DNS manipulation,
         network filtering, application-level blocking, or other
         technical interference — that blocks, filters, throttles,
         or degrades User access to the Official Free Pythos
         Service;

     (g) deliberately designing the product interface to make the
         Free Access Link difficult to find through visual
         deemphasis, misleading navigation structure, or
         intentional interface complexity; or

     (h) making any communication, policy, or practice — including
         verbal, written, or automated communications to Users —
         that discourages Users from accessing the Official Free
         Pythos Service through misrepresentation, false implication,
         or unfounded negative characterization.

3.4  PROHIBITED MISREPRESENTATION.

     An Operator must not make any affirmative statement to
     Users that is false or misleading regarding the free
     availability of Pythos. The following are prohibited:

     (a) stating or implying that payment is required to access
         Pythos, without immediately and prominently clarifying
         that free access is available at the Official Free
         Pythos Service;

     (b) stating or implying that there is no free version of
         Pythos;

     (c) stating or implying that the Operator's product is the
         official, only, or definitive version of Pythos;

     (d) stating or implying that the Official Free Pythos Service
         is unsafe, unreliable, discontinued, deprecated, or
         inferior in any respect that is not based on demonstrably
         accurate factual information that the Operator can
         substantiate; or

     (e) claiming official endorsement or affiliation with the
         Pythos project or copyright holder without written
         authorization.

3.5  PROHIBITED CRIPPLING.

     An Operator must not deliberately reduce the capabilities
     of a Covered Work below the documented capabilities of the
     Official Free Pythos Service for the purpose of making the
     commercial product appear superior by comparison to the
     Covered Work.

     The following acts create a rebuttable presumption of
     prohibited crippling:

     (a) reducing the mathematical accuracy, scope, or response
         quality of a Covered Work below the documented capability
         of the Official Free Pythos Service while simultaneously
         marketing the paid product's superior performance over
         that Covered Work; or

     (b) introducing artificial errors, deliberate delays, or
         artificial restrictions in a Covered Work that are not
         present in the Pythos codebase and that serve no
         legitimate technical purpose.

     The following are expressly NOT prohibited crippling:

     (c) a paid product providing additional proprietary features,
         better AI models, more subjects, faster response times,
         or other genuine enhancements not present in the
         Official Free Pythos Service;

     (d) a Covered Work operating at lower performance due to
         genuine infrastructure constraints, provided those
         constraints are not artificially introduced; or

     (e) maintaining a Covered Work that has not been updated
         to match every improvement in the Official Free Pythos
         Service, provided the Operator does not represent the
         Covered Work as current or equivalent to the Official
         Free Pythos Service.

3.6  SCOPE OF THESE OBLIGATIONS.

     These obligations apply to any Operator who distributes,
     hosts, deploys, or makes a Covered Work or Pythos Network
     Service available to Users, regardless of whether the
     Operator is a commercial company, nonprofit, school,
     university, government body, or individual.

     These obligations do NOT apply to:

     (a) private internal use of a Covered Work where no Users
         receive Pythos Functionality externally; or

     (b) use of Pythos solely to generate outputs (such as
         mathematical content or explanations) incorporated into
         separate works, without distributing or making available
         the Covered Work itself.

