SECTION 8. ATTRIBUTION
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

8.1  Any redistribution or public deployment of a Covered Work
     must:

     (a) preserve all copyright notices in the original Pythos
         source code;

     (b) include the following attribution in a location visible
         to Users — such as an About page, product interface, or
         documentation accessible without authentication:

             Based on Pythos
             Copyright (c) 2026 Jon Scott / LANZAR
             https://pythos.lanzar.me/
             Licensed under the Pythos Free Education License

     (c) not remove, alter, or obscure required attribution.

8.2  Attribution must be visible to Users without authentication
     or payment. Attribution placed exclusively in source code
     comments or inaccessible back-end documentation does not
     satisfy this requirement for deployed network services or
     distributed software.

